# /etc/synnet/trusted-networks — the networks this machine trusts.
#
# One NetworkManager connection per line: `<uuid> <name>`. The name is only a
# reminder; the uuid is what counts. `nmcli connection show` lists them.
#
# On a trusted network, other devices on it can reach this machine's services —
# file sharing, media servers, remote desktop. On any other network, only
# replies to connections this machine made, ping, DHCP and ports opened with
# `synnet --open` get in.
#
# Write it with `sudo synnet --trust-network <uuid|name>` (or --untrust-network),
# or Settings ▸ Network, which apply the change at once. Editing this file by
# hand takes effect at the next connection change, or `sudo synnet --firewall`.
